From 75a35e3d74c83081e4bac4b90b6b259d67fc4b60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remi Collet <remi@remirepo.net>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:08:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix for PHP 8.6.0beta3

  . The ZEND_RESULT_CODE type has been removed. Use zend_result directly.

  . The zval_dtor() alias of zval_ptr_dtor_nogc() has been removed.
    Call zval_ptr_dtor_nogc() directly instead.

  . The following PHP stream functions prefixed with _ have been removed,
    and the macro without it has become the canonical function name:
    * _php_stream_read()
    * _php_stream_write()

  . Extended php_stream_filter_ops with seek method.

  . zend_function.arg_info is now always a zend_arg_info*. Before, it was a
    zend_internal_arg_info on internal functions, unless the
    ZEND_ACC_USER_ARG_INFO flag was set.

(cherry picked from commit 0f0a17af21f8a2474742a8ace52b8a7b6112aba3)

[Rebased onto v4.3.1 by Chainguard: upstream commit 0f0a17af21 (m6w6/ext-http
master, 2026-09-17) replaces the ZEND_RESULT_CODE, zval_dtor() and XtOffsetOf()
uses PHP 8.6 removed. One context conflict in src/php_http_client_curl.c: the
master-only php_http_curlm_option_set_pipelining_bl() block does not exist in
4.3.1, so only the php_http_curlm_use_eventloop() return type is changed there.

Folded in, unchanged, are the two commits that follow it on upstream master
(same author, same day). They correct the arg_info code that 0f0a17af21 adds
to src/php_http_client_curl_user.c and src/php_http_client_curl_user.h:
  d5cf06cb58 "no default value": the handler's arguments have no default
    value, so strlen(NULL) crashed php_http_client_curl_user_init() on PHP 8.6.
  34ba4a66b8 "copy the 3 arginfo": the closure declares three arguments but
    was given the arg_info of one.
With them, these two files are those of upstream master at 34ba4a66b8.

Drop with the first release after 4.3.1.]
